The BED15 format is quite nice to represent alternative splicing events 
data (insertion/skipping), the grey scale of the score from the BED 
format is not ideal. Now, thanks to your implementation of BED15 format 
I  can update  the function for visualization of alternative splicing 
events in oneChannelGUI package.
Many thanks, again!
Raffaele

Michael Lawrence ha scritto:
> I guess we weren't sure if anyone wanted that, so it wasn't implemented. I
> just did though, for version 1.5.10. It's not documented yet, but you can do
> stuff like:
>
> track(session, format = "bed15", expNames = c("samp1", "samp2")) <- myTrack
>
> Where 'myTrack' has columns 'samp1' and 'samp2' containing expression
> values.
>
> Or to output every column, it's just:
>
> track(session, format = "bed15") <- myTrack
>
> If the track was imported from an external Bed15 track, then it's automatic:
> track(session) <- myTrack
>
> Hope this works for you,
> Michael
