Message-ID: <4A79FFC6.8080302@fhcrc.org>

Peng,
We don't have any utility to check the version numbers of all installed 
packages because as long as you don't install the development version of 
BioC with the release version of R and you routinely run the commands

biocLite(<<character vector of package names>>)

to install packages and

update.packages(repos = biocinstallRepos())

to update the BioC packages you will be current for your version of R.

Could you put your current situation in context? How have you been 
managing your packages and what is the current state of your R installation?


Patrick



